(window.IND_GITA_V = window.IND_GITA_V || {})[6] = [{"v":1,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":"श्री भगवानुवाच","spp":"before","sa":"अनाश्रितः कर्मफलं कार्यं कर्म करोति यः ।\nस संन्यासी च योगी च न निरग्निर्न चाक्रियः ॥","iast":"anāśritaḥ karmaphalaṃ kāryaṃ karma karoti yaḥ |\nsa saṃnyāsī ca yogī ca na niragnirna cākriyaḥ ||","read":"anaashritah karmaphalam kaaryam karma karoti yah |\nsa samnyaasee cha yogee cha na niragnirna chaakriyah ||","spli":"śrī bhagavānuvāca","splr":"shree bhagavaanuvaacha","en":"The Blessed Lord said: He that performeth such action as his duty, independently of the fruit of action, he is an ascetic, he is a Yogî, not he that is without fire, and without rites.","en2":"He who performs his bounden duty without leaning to the fruit of action —he is a renouncer of action as well as of steadfast mind: not he who is without fire, nor he who is without action.","en2r":null,"rv":null},{"v":2,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"यं संन्यासमिति प्राहुर्योगं तं विद्धि पाण्डव ।\nन ह्यसंन्यस्तसङ्कल्पो योगी भवति कश्चन ॥","iast":"yaṃ saṃnyāsamiti prāhuryogaṃ taṃ viddhi pāṇḍava |\nna hyasaṃnyastasaṅkalpo yogī bhavati kaścana ||","read":"yam samnyaasamiti praahuryogam tam viddhi paandava |\nna hyasamnyastasankalpo yogee bhavati kashchana ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"That which is called renunciation, know thou that as yoga, O Pândava; nor doth any one become a Yogî with the formative will unrenounced.","en2":"Know that to be devotion to action, which is called renunciation, O Pândava, for none becomes a devotee to action without forsaking Sankalpa.","en2r":null,"rv":null},{"v":3,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"आरुरुक्षोर्मुनेर्योगं कर्म कारणमुच्यते ।\nयोगारूढस्य तस्यैव शमः कारणमुच्यते ॥","iast":"ārurukṣormuneryogaṃ karma kāraṇamucyate |\nyogārūḍhasya tasyaiva śamaḥ kāraṇamucyate ||","read":"aarurukshormuneryogam karma kaaranamuchyate |\nyogaaroodhasya tasyaiva shamah kaaranamuchyate ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"For a Sage who is seeking Yoga, action is called the means; for the same Sage, when he is enthroned in yoga, serenity is called the means.","en2":"For the man of meditation wishing to attain purification of heart leading to concentration, work is said to be the way: For him, when he has attained such (concentration), inaction is said to be the way.","en2r":null,"rv":null},{"v":4,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"यदा हि नेन्द्रियार्थेषु न कर्मस्वनुषज्जते ।\nसर्वसङ्कल्पसंन्यासी योगारूढस्तदोच्यते ॥","iast":"yadā hi nendriyārtheṣu na karmasvanuṣajjate |\nsarvasaṅkalpasaṃnyāsī yogārūḍhastadocyate ||","read":"yadaa hi nendriyaartheshu na karmasvanushajjate |\nsarvasankalpasamnyaasee yogaaroodhastadochyate ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"When a man feeleth no attachment either for the objects of sense or for actions, renouncing the formative will, then, he is said to be enthroned in yoga.","en2":"Verily, when there is no attachment, either to sense-objects, or to actions, having renounced all Sankalpas, then is one said to have attained concentration.","en2r":null,"rv":null},{"v":5,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"उद्धरेदात्मनाऽऽत्मानं नात्मानमवसादयेत् ।\nआत्मैव ह्यात्मनो बन्धुरात्मैव रिपुरात्मनः ॥","iast":"uddharedātmanā’’tmānaṃ nātmānamavasādayet |\nātmaiva hyātmano bandhurātmaiva ripurātmanaḥ ||","read":"uddharedaatmanaa''tmaanam naatmaanamavasaadayet |\naatmaiva hyaatmano bandhuraatmaiva ripuraatmanah ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Let him raise the self by the Self and not let the self become depressed; for verily is the Self the friend of the self, and also the Self the self's enemy;","en2":"A man should uplift himself by his own self, so let him not weaken this self. For this self is the friend of oneself, and this self is the enemy of oneself.","en2r":null,"rv":null},{"v":6,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"बन्धुरात्माऽऽत्मनस्तस्य येनात्मैवात्मना जितः ।\nअनात्मनस्तु शत्रुत्वे वर्तेतात्मैव शत्रुवत् ॥","iast":"bandhurātmā’’tmanastasya yenātmaivātmanā jitaḥ |\nanātmanastu śatrutve vartetātmaiva śatruvat ||","read":"bandhuraatmaa''tmanastasya yenaatmaivaatmanaa jitah |\nanaatmanastu shatrutve vartetaatmaiva shatruvat ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"The Self is the friend of the self of him in whom the self by the Self is vanquished; but to the unsubdued self the Self verily becometh hostile as an enemy.","en2":"The self (the active part of our nature) is the friend of the self, for him who has conquered himself by this self. But to the unconquered self, this self is inimical, (and behaves) like (an external) foe.","en2r":null,"rv":null},{"v":7,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"जितात्मनः प्रशान्तस्य परमात्मा समाहितः ।\nशीतोष्णसुखदुःखेषु तथा मानापमानयोः ॥","iast":"jitātmanaḥ praśāntasya paramātmā samāhitaḥ |\nśītoṣṇasukhaduḥkheṣu tathā mānāpamānayoḥ ||","read":"jitaatmanah prashaantasya paramaatmaa samaahitah |\nsheetoshnasukhaduhkheshu tathaa maanaapamaanayoh ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"The higher Self of him who is Self -controlled and peaceful is uniform in cold and heat, pleasure and pain, as well as in honour and dishonour.","en2":"To the self-controlled and serene, the Supreme Self is, the object of constant, realisation, in cold and heat, pleasure and pain, as well as in honour and dishonour.","en2r":null,"rv":null},{"v":8,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"ज्ञानविज्ञानतृप्तात्मा कूटस्थो विजितेन्द्रियः ।\nयुक्त इत्युच्यते योगी समलोष्टाश्मकाञ्चनः ॥","iast":"jñānavijñānatṛptātmā kūṭastho vijitendriyaḥ |\nyukta ityucyate yogī samaloṣṭāśmakāñcanaḥ ||","read":"jnaanavijnaanatriptaatmaa kootastho vijitendriyah |\nyukta ityuchyate yogee samaloshtaashmakaanchanah ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"The Yogî who is satisfied with wisdom and knowledge, unwavering, whose senses are sub dued, to whom a lump of earth, a stone and gold are the same, is said to be harmonised.","en2":"Whose heart is filled with satisfaction by wisdom and realisation, and is changeless, whose senses are conquered, and to whom a lump of earth, stone, and gold are the same: that Yogi is called steadfast.","en2r":null,"rv":null},{"v":9,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"सुहृन्मित्रार्युदासीनमध्यस्थद्वेष्यबन्धुषु ।\nसाधुष्वपि च पापेषु समबुद्धिर्विशिष्यते ॥","iast":"suhṛnmitrāryudāsīnamadhyasthadveṣyabandhuṣu |\nsādhuṣvapi ca pāpeṣu samabuddhirviśiṣyate ||","read":"suhrinmitraaryudaaseenamadhyasthadveshyabandhushu |\nsaadhushvapi cha paapeshu samabuddhirvishishyate ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"He who regards impartially lovers, friends, and foes, strangers, neutrals, foreigners and relatives, also the righteous and unrighteous, he excelleth.","en2":"He attains excellence who looks with equal regard upon well-wishers, friends, foes, neutrals, arbiters, the hateful, the relatives, and upon the righteous and the unrighteous alike.","en2r":null,"rv":null},{"v":10,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"योगी युञ्जीत सततमात्मानं रहसि स्थितः ।\nएकाकी यतचित्तात्मा निराशीरपरिग्रहः ॥","iast":"yogī yuñjīta satatamātmānaṃ rahasi sthitaḥ |\nekākī yatacittātmā nirāśīraparigrahaḥ ||","read":"yogee yunjeeta satatamaatmaanam rahasi sthitah |\nekaakee yatachittaatmaa niraasheeraparigrahah ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Let the Yogî constantly engage himself in yoga, remaining in a secret place by himself, with thought and self subdued, free from hope and greed.","en2":"The Yogi should constantly practise concentration of the heart, retiring into solitude, alone, with the mind and body subdued, and free from hope and possession.","en2r":null,"rv":null},{"v":11,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"शुचौ देशे प्रतिष्ठाप्य स्थिरमासनमात्मनः ।\nनात्युच्छ्रितं नातिनीचं चैलाजिनकुशोत्तरम् ॥","iast":"śucau deśe pratiṣṭhāpya sthiramāsanamātmanaḥ |\nnātyucchritaṃ nātinīcaṃ cailājinakuśottaram ||","read":"shuchau deshe pratishthaapya sthiramaasanamaatmanah |\nnaatyuchchhritam naatineecham chailaajinakushottaram ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"In a pure place, established on a fixed seat of his own, neither very much raised nor very low, made of a cloth, a black antelope skin, and kusha grass, one over the other;","en2":"Having in a cleanly spot established his seat, firm, neither too high nor too low, made of a cloth, a skin, and Kusha-grass, arranged in consecution:","en2r":null,"rv":null},{"v":12,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"तत्रैकाग्रं मनः कृत्वा यतचित्तेन्द्रियक्रियः ।\nउपविश्यासने युञ्ज्याद्योगमात्मविशुद्धये ॥","iast":"tatraikāgraṃ manaḥ kṛtvā yatacittendriyakriyaḥ |\nupaviśyāsane yuñjyādyogamātmaviśuddhaye ||","read":"tatraikaagram manah kritvaa yatachittendriyakriyah |\nupavishyaasane yunjyaadyogamaatmavishuddhaye ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"There, having made the mind one-pointed, with thought and the functions of the senses subdued, steady on his seat, he should practise yoga for the purification of the self.","en2":"There, seated on that seat, making the mind one-pointed and subduing the action of the imaging faculty and the senses, let him practise Yoga for the purification of the heart.","en2r":null,"rv":null},{"v":13,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"समं कायशिरोग्रीवं धारयन्नचलं स्थिरः ।\nसंप्रेक्ष्य नासिकाग्रं स्वं दिशश्चानवलोकयन् ॥","iast":"samaṃ kāyaśirogrīvaṃ dhārayannacalaṃ sthiraḥ |\nsaṃprekṣya nāsikāgraṃ svaṃ diśaścānavalokayan ||","read":"samam kaayashirogreevam dhaarayannachalam sthirah |\nsamprekshya naasikaagram svam dishashchaanavalokayan ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Holding the body, head and neck erect, immovably steady, looking fixedly at the point of the nose, with unseeing gaze,","en2":"Let him firmly hold his body, head and neck erect and still, (with the eye-balls fixed, as if) gazing at the tip of his nose, and not looking around.","en2r":null,"rv":null},{"v":14,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"प्रशान्तात्मा विगतभीर्ब्रह्मचारिव्रते स्थितः ।\nमनः संयम्य मच्चित्तो युक्त आसीत मत्परः ॥","iast":"praśāntātmā vigatabhīrbrahmacārivrate sthitaḥ |\nmanaḥ saṃyamya maccitto yukta āsīta matparaḥ ||","read":"prashaantaatmaa vigatabheerbrahmachaarivrate sthitah |\nmanah samyamya machchitto yukta aaseeta matparah ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"The self serene, fearless, firm in the vow of the Brahmachâri, the mind controlled, thinking on Me, harmonised, let him sit aspiring after Me.","en2":"With the heart serene and fearless, firm in the vow of a Brahmachâri, with the mind controlled, and ever thinking of Me, let him sit (in Yoga) having Me as his supreme goal.","en2r":null,"rv":null},{"v":15,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"युञ्जन्नेवं सदाऽऽत्मानं योगी नियतमानसः ।\nशान्तिं निर्वाणपरमां मत्संस्थामधिगच्छति ॥","iast":"yuñjannevaṃ sadā’’tmānaṃ yogī niyatamānasaḥ |\nśāntiṃ nirvāṇaparamāṃ matsaṃsthāmadhigacchati ||","read":"yunjannevam sadaa''tmaanam yogee niyatamaanasah |\nshaantim nirvaanaparamaam matsamsthaamadhigachchhati ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"The Yogî ever united thus with the Self, with the mind controlled, goeth to Peace, to the supreme Bliss that abideth in Me.","en2":"Thus always keeping the mind steadfast, the Yogi of subdued mind attains the peace residing in Me,—the peace which culminates in Nirvâna (Moksha).","en2r":null,"rv":null},{"v":16,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"नात्यश्नतस्तु योगोऽस्ति न चैकान्तमनश्नतः ।\nन चातिस्वप्नशीलस्य जाग्रतो नैव चार्जुन ॥","iast":"nātyaśnatastu yogo’sti na caikāntamanaśnataḥ |\nna cātisvapnaśīlasya jāgrato naiva cārjuna ||","read":"naatyashnatastu yogo'sti na chaikaantamanashnatah |\nna chaatisvapnasheelasya jaagrato naiva chaarjuna ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Verily yoga is not for him who eateth too much, nor who abstaineth to excess, nor who is too much addicted to sleep, nor even to wakefulness, O Arjuna.","en2":"(Success in) Yoga is not for him who eats too much or too little—nor, O Arjuna, for him who sleeps too much or too little.","en2r":null,"rv":null},{"v":17,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"युक्ताहारविहारस्य युक्तचेष्टस्य कर्मसु ।\nयुक्तस्वप्नावबोधस्य योगो भवति दुःखहा ॥","iast":"yuktāhāravihārasya yuktaceṣṭasya karmasu |\nyuktasvapnāvabodhasya yogo bhavati duḥkhahā ||","read":"yuktaahaaravihaarasya yuktacheshtasya karmasu |\nyuktasvapnaavabodhasya yogo bhavati duhkhahaa ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Yoga killeth out all pain for him who is regulated in eating and amusement, regulated in performing actions, regulated in sleeping and waking.","en2":"To him who is temperate in eating and recreation, in his effort for work, and in sleep and wakefulness, Yoga becomes the destroyer of misery.","en2r":null,"rv":null},{"v":18,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"यदा विनियतं चित्तमात्मन्येवावतिष्ठते ।\nनिःस्पृहः सर्वकामेभ्यो युक्त इत्युच्यते तदा ॥","iast":"yadā viniyataṃ cittamātmanyevāvatiṣṭhate |\nniḥspṛhaḥ sarvakāmebhyo yukta ityucyate tadā ||","read":"yadaa viniyatam chittamaatmanyevaavatishthate |\nnihsprihah sarvakaamebhyo yukta ityuchyate tadaa ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"When his subdued thought is fixed on the Self, free from longing after all desirable things, then it is said, \"he is harmonised.\"","en2":"When the completely controlled mind rests serenely in the Self alone, free from longing after all desires, then is one called steadfast, (in the Self).","en2r":null,"rv":null},{"v":19,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"यथा दीपो निवातस्थो नेङ्गते सोपमा स्मृता ।\nयोगिनो यतचित्तस्य युञ्जतो योगमात्मनः ॥","iast":"yathā dīpo nivātastho neṅgate sopamā smṛtā |\nyogino yatacittasya yuñjato yogamātmanaḥ ||","read":"yathaa deepo nivaatastho nengate sopamaa smritaa |\nyogino yatachittasya yunjato yogamaatmanah ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"As a lamp in a windless place flickereth not, to such is likened the Yogî of subdued thought, absorbed in the yoga of the Self.","en2":"\"As a lamp in a spot sheltered from the wind does not flicker,\"—even such has been the simile used for a Yogi of subdued mind, practising concentration in the Self.","en2r":null,"rv":null},{"v":20,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"यत्रोपरमते चित्तं निरुद्धं योगसेवया ।\nयत्र चैवात्मनाऽऽत्मानं पश्यन्नात्मनि तुष्यति ॥","iast":"yatroparamate cittaṃ niruddhaṃ yogasevayā |\nyatra caivātmanā’’tmānaṃ paśyannātmani tuṣyati ||","read":"yatroparamate chittam niruddham yogasevayaa |\nyatra chaivaatmanaa''tmaanam pashyannaatmani tushyati ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"That in which the mind finds rest, quieted by the practice of yoga: that in which he, seeing the Self by the Self, in the Self is satisfied;","en2":"When the mind, absolutely restrained by the practice of concentration, attains quietude, and when seeing the Self by the self, one is satisfied in his own Self; when he feels that infinite bliss—which is perceived by the (purified) intellect and which transcends the senses, and established wherein he never departs from his real state; and having obtained which, regards no other acquisition superior to that, and where established, he is not moved even by heavy sorrow;—let that be known as the state, called by the name of Yoga,—a state of severance from the contact of pain. This Yoga should be practised with perseverance, undisturbed by depression of heart.","en2r":"6.20-23","rv":null},{"v":21,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"सुखमात्यन्तिकं यत्तद्बुद्धिग्राह्यमतीन्द्रियम् ।\nवेत्ति यत्र न चैवायं स्थितश्चलति तत्त्वतः ॥","iast":"sukhamātyantikaṃ yattadbuddhigrāhyamatīndriyam |\nvetti yatra na caivāyaṃ sthitaścalati tattvataḥ ||","read":"sukhamaatyantikam yattadbuddhigraahyamateendriyam |\nvetti yatra na chaivaayam sthitashchalati tattvatah ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"That in which he findeth the supreme delight which the Reason can grasp beyond the senses, wherein established he moveth not from the Reality;","en2":"When the mind, absolutely restrained by the practice of concentration, attains quietude, and when seeing the Self by the self, one is satisfied in his own Self; when he feels that infinite bliss—which is perceived by the (purified) intellect and which transcends the senses, and established wherein he never departs from his real state; and having obtained which, regards no other acquisition superior to that, and where established, he is not moved even by heavy sorrow;—let that be known as the state, called by the name of Yoga,—a state of severance from the contact of pain. This Yoga should be practised with perseverance, undisturbed by depression of heart.","en2r":"6.20-23","rv":null},{"v":22,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"यं लब्ध्वा चापरं लाभं मन्यते नाधिकं ततः ।\nयस्मिन्स्थितो न दुःखेन गुरुणापि विचाल्यते ॥","iast":"yaṃ labdhvā cāparaṃ lābhaṃ manyate nādhikaṃ tataḥ |\nyasminsthito na duḥkhena guruṇāpi vicālyate ||","read":"yam labdhvaa chaaparam laabham manyate naadhikam tatah |\nyasminsthito na duhkhena gurunaapi vichaalyate ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Which, having obtained, he thinketh there is no greater gain beyond it; wherein, established, he is not shaken even by heavy sorrow;","en2":"When the mind, absolutely restrained by the practice of concentration, attains quietude, and when seeing the Self by the self, one is satisfied in his own Self; when he feels that infinite bliss—which is perceived by the (purified) intellect and which transcends the senses, and established wherein he never departs from his real state; and having obtained which, regards no other acquisition superior to that, and where established, he is not moved even by heavy sorrow;—let that be known as the state, called by the name of Yoga,—a state of severance from the contact of pain. This Yoga should be practised with perseverance, undisturbed by depression of heart.","en2r":"6.20-23","rv":null},{"v":23,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"तं विद्याद् दुःखसंयोगवियोगं योगसंज्ञितम् ।\nस निश्चयेन योक्तव्यो योगोऽनिर्विण्णचेतसा ॥","iast":"taṃ vidyād duḥkhasaṃyogaviyogaṃ yogasaṃjñitam |\nsa niścayena yoktavyo yogo’nirviṇṇacetasā ||","read":"tam vidyaad duhkhasamyogaviyogam yogasamjnitam |\nsa nishchayena yoktavyo yogo'nirvinnachetasaa ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"That should be known by the name of yoga, this disconnection from the union with pain. This yoga must be clung to with a firm conviction and with undesponding mind.","en2":"When the mind, absolutely restrained by the practice of concentration, attains quietude, and when seeing the Self by the self, one is satisfied in his own Self; when he feels that infinite bliss—which is perceived by the (purified) intellect and which transcends the senses, and established wherein he never departs from his real state; and having obtained which, regards no other acquisition superior to that, and where established, he is not moved even by heavy sorrow;—let that be known as the state, called by the name of Yoga,—a state of severance from the contact of pain. This Yoga should be practised with perseverance, undisturbed by depression of heart.","en2r":"6.20-23","rv":null},{"v":24,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"सङ्कल्पप्रभवान्कामांस्त्यक्त्वा सर्वानशेषतः ।\nमनसैवेन्द्रियग्रामं विनियम्य समन्ततः ॥","iast":"saṅkalpaprabhavānkāmāṃstyaktvā sarvānaśeṣataḥ |\nmanasaivendriyagrāmaṃ viniyamya samantataḥ ||","read":"sankalpaprabhavaankaamaamstyaktvaa sarvaanasheshatah |\nmanasaivendriyagraamam viniyamya samantatah ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Abandoning without reserve all desires born of the imagination, by the mind curbing in the aggregate of the senses on every side,","en2":"Abandoning without reserve all desires born of Sankalpa, and completely restraining, by the mind alone, the whole group of senses from their objects in all directions;","en2r":null,"rv":null},{"v":25,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"शनैः शनैरुपरमेद् बुद्ध्या धृतिगृहीतया ।\nआत्मसंस्थं मनः कृत्वा न किञ्चिदपि चिन्तयेत् ॥","iast":"śanaiḥ śanairuparamed buddhyā dhṛtigṛhītayā |\nātmasaṃsthaṃ manaḥ kṛtvā na kiñcidapi cintayet ||","read":"shanaih shanairuparamed buddhyaa dhritigriheetayaa |\naatmasamstham manah kritvaa na kinchidapi chintayet ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Little by little let him gain tranquillity, by means of Reason controlled by steadiness; having made the mind abide in the Self, let him not think of anything.","en2":"With the intellect set in patience, with the mind fastened on the Self, let him attain quietude by degrees: let him not think of anything.","en2r":null,"rv":null},{"v":26,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"यतो यतो निश्चरति मनश्चञ्चलमस्थिरम् ।\nततस्ततो नियम्यैतदात्मन्येव वशं नयेत् ॥","iast":"yato yato niścarati manaścañcalamasthiram |\ntatastato niyamyaitadātmanyeva vaśaṃ nayet ||","read":"yato yato nishcharati manashchanchalamasthiram |\ntatastato niyamyaitadaatmanyeva vasham nayet ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"As often as the wavering and unsteady mind goeth forth, so often reining it in, let him bring it under the control of the Self.","en2":"Through whatever reason the restless, unsteady mind wanders away, let him curbing it from that, bring it under the subjugation of the Self alone.","en2r":null,"rv":null},{"v":27,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"प्रशान्तमनसं ह्येनं योगिनं सुखमुत्तमम् ।\nउपैति शान्तरजसं ब्रह्मभूतमकल्मषम् ॥","iast":"praśāntamanasaṃ hyenaṃ yoginaṃ sukhamuttamam |\nupaiti śāntarajasaṃ brahmabhūtamakalmaṣam ||","read":"prashaantamanasam hyenam yoginam sukhamuttamam |\nupaiti shaantarajasam brahmabhootamakalmasham ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Supreme joy is for this Yogi whose mind is peaceful, whose passion-nature is calmed, who is sinless and of the nature of the Eternal.","en2":"Verily, the supreme bliss comes to that Yogi, of perfectly tranquil mind, with passions quieted, Brahman-become, and freed from taint.","en2r":null,"rv":null},{"v":28,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"युञ्जन्नेवं सदाऽऽत्मानं योगी विगतकल्मषः ।\nसुखेन ब्रह्मसंस्पर्शमत्यन्तं सुखमश्नुते ॥","iast":"yuñjannevaṃ sadā’’tmānaṃ yogī vigatakalmaṣaḥ |\nsukhena brahmasaṃsparśamatyantaṃ sukhamaśnute ||","read":"yunjannevam sadaa''tmaanam yogee vigatakalmashah |\nsukhena brahmasamsparshamatyantam sukhamashnute ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"The Yogî who thus, ever harmonising the self, hath put away sin, he easily enjoyeth the infinite bliss of contact with the Eternal.","en2":"The Yogi freed from taint (of good and evil), constantly engaging the mind thus, with ease attains the infinite bliss of contact with Brahman.","en2r":null,"rv":null},{"v":29,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"सर्वभूतस्थमात्मानं सर्वभूतानि चात्मनि ।\nईक्षते योगयुक्तात्मा सर्वत्र समदर्शनः ॥","iast":"sarvabhūtasthamātmānaṃ sarvabhūtāni cātmani |\nīkṣate yogayuktātmā sarvatra samadarśanaḥ ||","read":"sarvabhootasthamaatmaanam sarvabhootaani chaatmani |\neekshate yogayuktaatmaa sarvatra samadarshanah ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"The self, harmonised by yoga, seeth the Self abiding in all beings, all beings in the Self; everywhere he seeth the same.","en2":"With the heart concentrated by Yoga, with the eye of evenness for all things, he beholds the Self in all beings and all beings in the Self.","en2r":null,"rv":null},{"v":30,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"यो मां पश्यति सर्वत्र सर्वं च मयि पश्यति ।\nतस्याहं न प्रणश्यामि स च मे न प्रणश्यति ॥","iast":"yo māṃ paśyati sarvatra sarvaṃ ca mayi paśyati |\ntasyāhaṃ na praṇaśyāmi sa ca me na praṇaśyati ||","read":"yo maam pashyati sarvatra sarvam cha mayi pashyati |\ntasyaaham na pranashyaami sa cha me na pranashyati ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"He who seeth Me everywhere, and seeth everything in Me, of him will I never lose hold, and he shall never lose hold of Me.","en2":"He who sees Me in all things, and sees all things in Me, he never becomes separated from Me, nor do I become separated from him.","en2r":null,"rv":null},{"v":31,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"सर्वभूतस्थितं यो मां भजत्येकत्वमास्थितः ।\nसर्वथा वर्तमानोऽपि स योगी मयि वर्तते ॥","iast":"sarvabhūtasthitaṃ yo māṃ bhajatyekatvamāsthitaḥ |\nsarvathā vartamāno’pi sa yogī mayi vartate ||","read":"sarvabhootasthitam yo maam bhajatyekatvamaasthitah |\nsarvathaa vartamaano'pi sa yogee mayi vartate ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"He who, established in unity, worshippeth Me abiding in all beings, that Yogi liveth in Me, whatever his mode of living.","en2":"He who being established in unity, worships Me, who am dwelling in all beings, whatever his mode of life, that Yogi abides in Me.","en2r":null,"rv":null},{"v":32,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"आत्मौपम्येन सर्वत्र समं पश्यति योऽर्जुन ।\nसुखं वा यदि वा दुःखं स योगी परमो मतः ॥","iast":"ātmaupamyena sarvatra samaṃ paśyati yo’rjuna |\nsukhaṃ vā yadi vā duḥkhaṃ sa yogī paramo mataḥ ||","read":"aatmaupamyena sarvatra samam pashyati yo'rjuna |\nsukham vaa yadi vaa duhkham sa yogee paramo matah ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"He who, through the likeness of the Self, O Arjuna, seeth equality in everything, whether pleasant or painful, he is considered a perfect Yogî.","en2":"He who judges of pleasure or pain everywhere, by the same standard as he applies to himself, that Yogi, O Arjuna, is regarded as the highest.","en2r":null,"rv":null},{"v":33,"sp":"arjuna","spm":null,"spl":"अर्जुन उवाच","spp":"before","sa":"योऽयं योगस्त्वया प्रोक्तः साम्येन मधुसूदन ।\nएतस्याहं न पश्यामि चञ्चलत्वात् स्थितिं स्थिराम् ॥","iast":"yo’yaṃ yogastvayā proktaḥ sāmyena madhusūdana |\netasyāhaṃ na paśyāmi cañcalatvāt sthitiṃ sthirām ||","read":"yo'yam yogastvayaa proktah saamyena madhusoodana |\netasyaaham na pashyaami chanchalatvaat sthitim sthiraam ||","spli":"arjuna uvāca","splr":"arjuna uvaacha","en":"This yoga which Thou hast declared to be by equanimity, O Madhusûdana, I see not a stable foundation for it, owing to restlessness;","en2":"This Yoga which has been taught by Thee, O slayer of Madhu, as characterised by evenness, I do not see (the possibility of) its lasting endurance, owing to restlessness (of the mind).","en2r":null,"rv":null},{"v":34,"sp":"arjuna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"चञ्चलं हि मनः कृष्ण प्रमाथि बलवद्दृढम् ।\nतस्याहं निग्रहं मन्ये वायोरिव सुदुष्करम् ॥","iast":"cañcalaṃ hi manaḥ kṛṣṇa pramāthi balavaddṛḍham |\ntasyāhaṃ nigrahaṃ manye vāyoriva suduṣkaram ||","read":"chanchalam hi manah krishna pramaathi balavaddridham |\ntasyaaham nigraham manye vaayoriva sudushkaram ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"For the mind is verily restless, O Krishna; it is impetuous, strong and difficult to bend. I deem it as hard to curb as the wind.","en2":"Verily, the mind, O Krishna, is restless, turbulent, strong, and unyielding;. I regard it quite as hard to achieve its control, as that of the wind.","en2r":null,"rv":null},{"v":35,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":"श्री भगवानुवाच","spp":"before","sa":"असंशयं महाबाहो मनो दुर्निग्रहं चलम् ।\nअभ्यासेन तु कौन्तेय वैराग्येण च गृह्यते ॥","iast":"asaṃśayaṃ mahābāho mano durnigrahaṃ calam |\nabhyāsena tu kaunteya vairāgyeṇa ca gṛhyate ||","read":"asamshayam mahaabaaho mano durnigraham chalam |\nabhyaasena tu kaunteya vairaagyena cha grihyate ||","spli":"śrī bhagavānuvāca","splr":"shree bhagavaanuvaacha","en":"The Blessed Lord said: Without doubt, O mighty-armed, the mind is hard to curb and restless; but it may be curbed by constant practice and by dispassion.","en2":"Without doubt, O mighty-armed, the mind is restless, and difficult to control; but through practice and renunciation, O son of Kunti, it may be governed.","en2r":null,"rv":null},{"v":36,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"असंयतात्मना योगो दुष्प्राप इति मे मतिः ।\nवश्यात्मना तु यतता शक्योऽवाप्तुमुपायतः ॥","iast":"asaṃyatātmanā yogo duṣprāpa iti me matiḥ |\nvaśyātmanā tu yatatā śakyo’vāptumupāyataḥ ||","read":"asamyataatmanaa yogo dushpraapa iti me matih |\nvashyaatmanaa tu yatataa shakyo'vaaptumupaayatah ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Yoga is hard to attain, methinks, by a self that is uncontrolled; but by the Self -controlled it is attainable by properly directed energy.","en2":"Yoga is hard to be attained by one of uncontrolled self: such is My conviction; but the self-controlled, striving by right means, can obtain it.","en2r":null,"rv":null},{"v":37,"sp":"arjuna","spm":null,"spl":"अर्जुन उवाच","spp":"before","sa":"अयतिः श्रद्धयोपेतो योगाच्चलितमानसः ।\nअप्राप्य योगसंसिद्धिं कां गतिं कृष्ण गच्छति ॥","iast":"ayatiḥ śraddhayopeto yogāccalitamānasaḥ |\naprāpya yogasaṃsiddhiṃ kāṃ gatiṃ kṛṣṇa gacchati ||","read":"ayatih shraddhayopeto yogaachchalitamaanasah |\napraapya yogasamsiddhim kaam gatim krishna gachchhati ||","spli":"arjuna uvāca","splr":"arjuna uvaacha","en":"Arjuna said: He who is unsubdued but who possesseth faith, with the mind wandering away from yoga, failing to attain perfection in yoga, what path doth he tread, O Krishna?","en2":"Though possessed of Shraddhâ but unable to control himself, with the mind wandering away from Yoga, what end does one, failing to gain perfection in Yoga, meet, O Krishna?","en2r":null,"rv":null},{"v":38,"sp":"arjuna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"कच्चिन्नोभयविभ्रष्टश्छिन्नाभ्रमिव नश्यति ।\nअप्रतिष्ठो महाबाहो विमूढो ब्रह्मणः पथि ॥","iast":"kaccinnobhayavibhraṣṭaśchinnābhramiva naśyati |\napratiṣṭho mahābāho vimūḍho brahmaṇaḥ pathi ||","read":"kachchinnobhayavibhrashtashchhinnaabhramiva nashyati |\napratishtho mahaabaaho vimoodho brahmanah pathi ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Fallen from both, is he destroyed like a rent cloud, unsteadfast, O mighty-armed, deluded in the path of the Eternal?","en2":"Does he not, fallen from both, perish, without support, like a rent cloud, O mighty-armed, deluded in the path of Brahman?","en2r":null,"rv":null},{"v":39,"sp":"arjuna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"एतन्मे संशयं कृष्ण छेत्तुमर्हस्यशेषतः ।\nत्वदन्यः संशयस्यास्य छेत्ता न ह्युपपद्यते ॥","iast":"etanme saṃśayaṃ kṛṣṇa chettumarhasyaśeṣataḥ |\ntvadanyaḥ saṃśayasyāsya chettā na hyupapadyate ||","read":"etanme samshayam krishna chhettumarhasyasheshatah |\ntvadanyah samshayasyaasya chhettaa na hyupapadyate ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Deign, O Krishna, to completely dispel this doubt of mine; for there is none to be found save Thyself able to destroy this doubt.","en2":"This doubt of mine, O Krishna, Thou shouldst completely dispel; for it is not possible for any but Thee to dispel this doubt.","en2r":null,"rv":null},{"v":40,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":"श्री भगवानुवाच","spp":"before","sa":"पार्थ नैवेह नामुत्र विनाशस्तस्य विद्यते ।\nनहि कल्याणकृत्कश्चिद्दुर्गतिं तात गच्छति ॥","iast":"pārtha naiveha nāmutra vināśastasya vidyate |\nnahi kalyāṇakṛtkaściddurgatiṃ tāta gacchati ||","read":"paartha naiveha naamutra vinaashastasya vidyate |\nnahi kalyaanakritkashchiddurgatim taata gachchhati ||","spli":"śrī bhagavānuvāca","splr":"shree bhagavaanuvaacha","en":"The Blessed Lord said: O son of Prithâ, neither in this world nor in the life to come is there destruction for him; never doth any who worketh righteousness, O beloved, tread the path of woe.","en2":"Verily, O son of Prithâ, there is destruction for him, neither here nor hereafter: for, the doer of good, O my son, never comes to grief.","en2r":null,"rv":null},{"v":41,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"प्राप्य पुण्यकृतां लोकानुषित्वा शाश्वतीः समाः ।\nशुचीनां श्रीमतां गेहे योगभ्रष्टोऽभिजायते ॥","iast":"prāpya puṇyakṛtāṃ lokānuṣitvā śāśvatīḥ samāḥ |\nśucīnāṃ śrīmatāṃ gehe yogabhraṣṭo’bhijāyate ||","read":"praapya punyakritaam lokaanushitvaa shaashvateeh samaah |\nshucheenaam shreemataam gehe yogabhrashto'bhijaayate ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Having attained to the worlds of the pure-doing, and having dwelt there for immemorial years, he who fell from yoga is reborn in a pure and blessed house;","en2":"Having attained to the worlds of the righteous, and dwelling there for everlasting years, one fallen from Yoga reincarnates in the home of the pure and the prosperous.","en2r":null,"rv":null},{"v":42,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"अथवा योगिनामेव कुले भवति धीमताम् ।\nएतद्धि दुर्लभतरं लोके जन्म यदीदृशम् ॥","iast":"athavā yogināmeva kule bhavati dhīmatām |\netaddhi durlabhataraṃ loke janma yadīdṛśam ||","read":"athavaa yoginaameva kule bhavati dheemataam |\netaddhi durlabhataram loke janma yadeedrisham ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Or he may even be born into a family of wise Yogîs; but such a birth as that is most difficult to obtain in this world.","en2":"Or else he is born into a family of wise Yogis only; verily, a birth such as that is very rare to obtain in this world.","en2r":null,"rv":null},{"v":43,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"तत्र तं बुद्धिसंयोगं लभते पौर्वदेहिकम् ।\nयतते च ततो भूयः संसिद्धौ कुरुनन्दन ॥","iast":"tatra taṃ buddhisaṃyogaṃ labhate paurvadehikam |\nyatate ca tato bhūyaḥ saṃsiddhau kurunandana ||","read":"tatra tam buddhisamyogam labhate paurvadehikam |\nyatate cha tato bhooyah samsiddhau kurunandana ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"There he recovereth the characteristics belonging to this former body, and with these he again laboureth for perfection, O joy of the Kurus.","en2":"There he is united with the intelligence acquired in his former body, and strives more than before, for perfection, O son of the Kurus.","en2r":null,"rv":null},{"v":44,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"पूर्वाभ्यासेन तेनैव ह्रियते ह्यवशोऽपि सः ।\nजिज्ञासुरपि योगस्य शब्दब्रह्मातिवर्तते ॥","iast":"pūrvābhyāsena tenaiva hriyate hyavaśo’pi saḥ |\njijñāsurapi yogasya śabdabrahmātivartate ||","read":"poorvaabhyaasena tenaiva hriyate hyavasho'pi sah |\njijnaasurapi yogasya shabdabrahmaativartate ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"By that former practice he is irresistibly swept away. Only wishing to know yoga, even the seeker after yoga goeth beyond the Brâhmic world;","en2":"By that previous practice alone, he is borne on in spite of himself. Even the enquirer after Yoga rises superior to the performer of Vedic actions.","en2r":null,"rv":null},{"v":45,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"प्रयत्नाद्यतमानस्तु योगी संशुद्धकिल्बिषः ।\nअनेकजन्मसंसिद्धस्ततो याति परां गतिम् ॥","iast":"prayatnādyatamānastu yogī saṃśuddhakilbiṣaḥ |\nanekajanmasaṃsiddhastato yāti parāṃ gatim ||","read":"prayatnaadyatamaanastu yogee samshuddhakilbishah |\nanekajanmasamsiddhastato yaati paraam gatim ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"But the Yogî, labouring with assiduity, purified from sin, fully perfected through manifold births, he reacheth the supreme goal.","en2":"The Yogi, striving assiduously, purified of taint, gradually gaining perfection through many births, then reaches the highest goal.","en2r":null,"rv":null},{"v":46,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"तपस्विभ्योऽधिको योगी ज्ञानिभ्योऽपि मतोऽधिकः ।\nकर्मिभ्यश्चाधिको योगी तस्माद्योगी भवार्जुन ॥","iast":"tapasvibhyo’dhiko yogī jñānibhyo’pi mato’dhikaḥ |\nkarmibhyaścādhiko yogī tasmādyogī bhavārjuna ||","read":"tapasvibhyo'dhiko yogee jnaanibhyo'pi mato'dhikah |\nkarmibhyashchaadhiko yogee tasmaadyogee bhavaarjuna ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"The Yogî is greater than the ascetics; he is thought to be greater than even the wise; the Yogî is greater than the men of action; therefore become thou a Yogî, O Arjuna!","en2":"The Yogi is regarded as superior to those who practise asceticism, also to those who have obtained wisdom (through the Shâstras). He is also superior to the performers of action, (enjoined in the Vedas). Therefore, be thou a Yogi, O Arjuna!","en2r":null,"rv":null},{"v":47,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"योगिनामपि सर्वेषां मद्गतेनान्तरात्मना ।\nश्रद्धावान्भजते यो मां स मे युक्ततमो मतः ॥","iast":"yogināmapi sarveṣāṃ madgatenāntarātmanā |\nśraddhāvānbhajate yo māṃ sa me yuktatamo mataḥ ||","read":"yoginaamapi sarveshaam madgatenaantaraatmanaa |\nshraddhaavaanbhajate yo maam sa me yuktatamo matah ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"And among all Yogîs, he who, full of faith, with the inner Self abiding in Me, adoreth Me, he is considered by Me to be the most completely harmonised.","en2":"And of all Yogis, he who with the inner self merged in Me, with Shraddhâ devotes himself to Me, is considered by Me the most steadfast.","en2r":null,"rv":null}];
